{
  "target": "0.4.0",
  "gate": [
    "Every tier 1 and tier 1b feature passes on each surface that applies, and so does every acceptance criterion of their stories. This includes N1 to N4, so the UI consolidation is part of this release. Deferred only with a written reason.",
    "Tier 2 should work: an open item does not block the release, but the changelog names it as a known gap. Tier 3 may wait.",
    "Every requirement is met, or deferred with a reason. Outdated ones are rewritten.",
    "Every finding is fixed, or accepted with a reason. Accepted limits are stated in the README.",
    "The automated suites and `claude plugin validate` pass, and a manual run is recorded on all three surfaces.",
    "Real use is recorded: the author's own paper for at least 2 weeks, and a think-aloud with 2 to 3 researchers."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "The log is append-only by convention only: `ai-log/` is one of Claude's write places, is not on the sandbox deny list and is not an author file, so the comparison does not cover it",
      "evidence": "`CLAUDE_WRITES` in `plugin/hooks/core.ts`; the \"ok\" list in `plugin/tests/cowriting.test.tsx`; `plugin/templates/workspace/.claude/settings.json`",
      "why": "The README says append-only, and the disclosure is built from this log",
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Guard built and confirmed in a real session on 2026-11-05 (F15). Remaining limits are in the README"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "AI text is flagged only if the model marks it: unmarked prose in an answer is not detected",
      "evidence": "`e.answer.includes(AI_TEXT_MARKER)` in `plugin/hooks/register.tsx`",
      "why": "R1.1 and R1.4 depend on model behaviour, which has no tests today",
      "status": "open"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "No warning for confidential material: only a rule line in the workspace `CLAUDE.md` exists",
      "evidence": "Search over hooks, tools and template",
      "why": "R6.1 promises a warning",
      "status": "open"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "title": "No per-institution disclosure template: fixed text that says to adapt it, and the skill helps by hand",
      "evidence": "`plugin/tools/ailog.py`, disclosure skill",
      "why": "R4.2 is only partly met",
      "status": "open"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "title": "Two requirements are out of date: R1.3 forbids corrected sentences, R2.2 lets Claude write to `literature/`",
      "evidence": "`plugin/skills/language/SKILL.md`, `CLAUDE_WRITES`",
      "why": "The list contradicts the product",
      "status": "open"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "title": "The README overstates \"read-only\": each persona is called a read-only subagent, but 3 have Write and 3 have Bash",
      "evidence": "`plugin/agents/*.md`",
      "why": "Doc fix, and the guard must hold for these personas",
      "status": "open"
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "title": "Skill text has almost no automated coverage: 9 of the 11 skills checked are not named in the hook tests (`ailog.py` itself is tested)",
      "evidence": "Search by name in `plugin/tests/cowriting.test.tsx`; a rough check",
      "why": "These are the instructions behind most of the help the author sees",
      "status": "open"
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "title": "Small doc gaps: `/cowrite:paper versioning` is missing from the skill's hint and description; the README command table omits `m` (Remember)",
      "evidence": "`plugin/skills/paper/SKILL.md`, `README.md`",
      "why": "Discoverability",
      "status": "open"
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "title": "The guard can refuse harmless shell commands: a long script that only mentioned the word manuscript in its text, and wrote elsewhere, was refused during plugin development on 2026-11-05. The exact trigger is not yet pinned down",
      "evidence": "Observed in a session with the plugin installed; refusal text was the GUARD_MESSAGE of `plugin/hooks/core.ts`",
      "why": "False alarms teach authors and Claude to work around the guard. To reproduce under test type G",
      "status": "open"
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "title": "Refused attempts leave no trace: a refused write to the log or the author's files is not logged, and a refused tool is missing from the response's `tools_used`. The disclosure's heading *Attempts to change the AI log afterwards* therefore lists only rewrites that got through",
      "evidence": "Real session on 2026-11-05: steps 1 and 2 were refused, and the log has one guard entry (step 4) and `tools_used: [\"Bash\"]`",
      "why": "The author signs this. Either log refusals too, or word the heading so it does not read as complete",
      "status": "open"
    }
  ],
